1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,711
[CLEARS THROAT] <i>Um…</i>

2
00:00:05,255 --> 00:00:07,590
<i>Have some more, Oliver. Here.</i>

3
00:00:07,674 --> 00:00:10,385
<i>He can't. We're monitoring Oliver's diet.</i>

4
00:00:10,468 --> 00:00:11,678
<i>He has diabetes.</i>

5
00:00:11,761 --> 00:00:12,846
<i>Eat up.</i>

6
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:14,222
<i>Oh, right.</i>

7
00:00:14,305 --> 00:00:16,891
<i>- You have it, Pa.</i>
<i>- He's diabetic too.</i>

8
00:00:16,975 --> 00:00:19,561
<i>We're limiting his consumption of meat.</i>

9
00:00:21,563 --> 00:00:23,523
<i>You can have it.</i>

10
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:25,066
[CHUCKLES]

11
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:27,652
<i>Then I'll help myself.</i>

12
00:00:28,486 --> 00:00:31,239
<i>I love Auntie Precious's cooking.</i>

13
00:00:31,322 --> 00:00:33,324
<i>- It's delicious.</i>
<i>- Thank you.</i>

14
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:36,119
[BEA] <i>It's so good.</i>

15
00:00:36,202 --> 00:00:37,495
[BILLY] <i>Now, about Caloy…</i>

16
00:00:37,579 --> 00:00:39,831
<i>Do you know he escaped?</i>

17
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:42,333
<i>Huh?</i>

18
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:44,961
<i>You're no longer in touch?</i>

19
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:47,756
<i>N-N… No!</i>

20
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:51,217
[SCOFFS] <i>Billy, how would we get in touch?</i>

21
00:00:51,301 --> 00:00:53,970
<i>I don't have his number.</i>

22
00:00:54,054 --> 00:00:56,598
<i>We're… We're not…</i>
<i>We're not together, remember?</i>

23
00:00:56,681 --> 00:00:59,434
<i>But I hope he does contact me.</i>

24
00:01:00,518 --> 00:01:01,436
<i>What?</i>

25
00:01:02,687 --> 00:01:04,355
<i>I hope he contacts me</i>

26
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:07,984
<i>so I can then tell you,</i>
<i>and you can have him arrested.</i>

27
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:09,486
<i>Billy.</i>

28
00:01:09,569 --> 00:01:10,653
<i>I'm on your side.</i>

29
00:01:10,737 --> 00:01:16,034
<i>I will do everything I can</i>
<i>to help you catch that Caloy.</i>

30
00:01:17,118 --> 00:01:18,369
<i>I swear I'll do anything.</i>

31
00:01:19,204 --> 00:01:22,123
<i>Trust me, we're on the same side now.</i>

32
00:01:25,001 --> 00:01:26,211
[JORDAN] <i>We're still closed.</i>

33
00:01:26,294 --> 00:01:27,420
<i>Come back later.</i>

34
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:32,300
[SOFT, STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

35
00:01:34,177 --> 00:01:35,386
[DINO] <i>Can we talk?</i>

36
00:01:36,179 --> 00:01:37,847
<i>I've changed.</i>

37
00:01:37,931 --> 00:01:39,432
<i>I want to make it up to you.</i>

38
00:01:40,183 --> 00:01:41,601
<i>How are you going to do that?</i>

39
00:01:41,684 --> 00:01:42,977
<i>Look at you.</i>

40
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:45,104
<i>You're a fugitive.</i>

41
00:01:46,356 --> 00:01:51,111
[CLEARS THROAT]
<i>Um, aside from your forgiveness…</i>

42
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:56,032
<i>of course, I also need money</i>
<i>to start again.</i>

43
00:01:57,784 --> 00:01:58,993
<i>Just so we're clear.</i>

44
00:01:59,702 --> 00:02:00,995
<i>Really clear.</i>

45
00:02:01,496 --> 00:02:05,291
<i>Dad, you won't get any money from me.</i>

46
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:07,252
<i>Okay?</i>

47
00:02:09,087 --> 00:02:10,338
<i>You know,</i>

48
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:15,343
<i>you're so stingy for someone</i>
<i>who earns so much.</i>

49
00:02:20,807 --> 00:02:23,601
<i>I owe you nothing.</i>

50
00:02:25,645 --> 00:02:27,188
<i>My answer is no.</i>

51
00:02:27,897 --> 00:02:29,399
<i>Well, think again, hmm?</i>

52
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:33,069
<i>That song that made you famous?</i>

53
00:02:34,028 --> 00:02:35,780
<i>Who do you think</i>
<i>your mother wrote that for?</i>

54
00:02:35,864 --> 00:02:37,866
<i>For you? No.</i>

55
00:02:37,949 --> 00:02:40,660
<i>She wrote it for the two of us.</i>

56
00:02:41,828 --> 00:02:43,079
<i>It was for you too.</i>

57
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:47,625
<i>But that was before</i>
<i>you started hurting her.</i>

58
00:02:50,211 --> 00:02:54,507
<i>No matter what you say,</i>
<i>I deserve my share.</i>

59
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:56,885
<i>Get out.</i>

60
00:02:57,802 --> 00:02:59,053
<i>Excuse me?</i>

61
00:02:59,137 --> 00:03:01,097
<i>- Get out!</i>
<i>- No!</i>

62
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:02,891
<i>- If you don't leave…</i>
<i>- What?</i>

63
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:04,058
<i>I'm calling…</i>

64
00:03:04,142 --> 00:03:05,393
<i>Who? The cops?</i>

65
00:03:05,476 --> 00:03:08,354
<i>- Don't touch me! Get off me!</i>
<i>- You'll call the cops?</i>

66
00:03:08,438 --> 00:03:09,814
<i>- You bastard!</i>
- [BLOW LANDS]

67
00:03:10,607 --> 00:03:12,942
[GRUNTS]

68
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:18,781
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

69
00:03:27,665 --> 00:03:30,293
- [INHALES, GRUNTS ANGRILY]
- [SLAMS FLOOR]

70
00:03:38,927 --> 00:03:44,724
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

71
00:03:48,394 --> 00:03:49,479
Jordan?

72
00:03:55,318 --> 00:03:56,277
Jordan?

73
00:03:56,903 --> 00:03:57,779
Dude?

74
00:03:59,489 --> 00:04:00,573
[GROANS]

75
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,534
Why are you here?

76
00:04:04,118 --> 00:04:05,495
Who did that to you?

77
00:04:12,543 --> 00:04:19,509
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

78
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:25,074
Dad apologized to me.

79
00:05:29,454 --> 00:05:31,205
Then, he asked for money

80
00:05:32,206 --> 00:05:34,459
so he could start again.

81
00:05:36,627 --> 00:05:38,004
So, of course,

82
00:05:38,087 --> 00:05:39,338
I said no.

83
00:05:41,049 --> 00:05:42,425
He got mad at me.

84
00:05:42,925 --> 00:05:45,303
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

85
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:47,680
So I threatened
to call the police, and then…

86
00:05:48,890 --> 00:05:50,349
he punched me.

87
00:05:54,312 --> 00:05:55,480
Dude, you were right.

88
00:05:58,733 --> 00:06:00,610
I was wrong to hope

89
00:06:02,278 --> 00:06:03,780
he would change.

90
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:07,241
I didn't listen.

91
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:11,871
[SOBS]

92
00:06:15,249 --> 00:06:21,964
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

93
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:29,138
I only got my hopes up

94
00:06:30,515 --> 00:06:32,517
because I felt like

95
00:06:34,477 --> 00:06:36,395
he was all I had left.

96
00:06:38,815 --> 00:06:39,816
Mom is dead.

97
00:06:41,025 --> 00:06:42,401
Grandpa Jude…

98
00:06:42,902 --> 00:06:45,279
He's still alive,
but it's like he's not even here.

99
00:06:45,863 --> 00:06:47,490
It's just hard to accept…

100
00:06:49,325 --> 00:06:51,202
that he's the only family I have left.

101
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:53,162
And this is what happens.

102
00:06:54,664 --> 00:06:58,167
Why did I have to have
such a terrible father?

103
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:02,171
But you're not like him.

104
00:07:04,841 --> 00:07:05,967
Right?

105
00:07:07,093 --> 00:07:09,470
You're nothing like your father.

106
00:07:10,304 --> 00:07:13,057
Because you are better than him.

107
00:07:13,683 --> 00:07:17,353
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

108
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:19,313
There is nothing wrong

109
00:07:19,397 --> 00:07:23,818
with hoping that the people we love
will love us back.

110
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:26,112
- [JORDAN SNIFFLES]
- But…

111
00:07:29,532 --> 00:07:32,535
when you're getting hurt
over and over again,

112
00:07:33,953 --> 00:07:36,664
I have to draw the line.

113
00:07:38,207 --> 00:07:40,585
I won't let you do this anymore, okay?

114
00:07:41,711 --> 00:07:44,297
You don't need his love

115
00:07:45,715 --> 00:07:48,092
for you to feel complete.

116
00:07:49,218 --> 00:07:52,346
You were able to live without him.

117
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:55,975
And you can do it again
even if he leaves again.

118
00:07:57,351 --> 00:08:00,396
He will regret turning his back on you.

119
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:04,692
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

120
00:08:04,775 --> 00:08:06,027
[JORDAN SNIFFLES]

121
00:08:08,654 --> 00:08:09,697
[JORDAN SNIFFLES]

122
00:08:13,367 --> 00:08:15,161
[JORDAN SNIFFLES, SIGHS]

123
00:08:20,291 --> 00:08:25,296
And it's not true that
he's the only one you have left.

124
00:08:26,339 --> 00:08:28,257
That you don't have
anyone on your side anymore.

125
00:08:33,137 --> 00:08:34,680
I'm here.

126
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:41,479
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

127
00:08:56,744 --> 00:09:01,874
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

128
00:09:06,796 --> 00:09:13,427
["AAMININ" BY JAMES REID
AND KATHRYN BERNARDO PLAYING]

129
00:09:28,776 --> 00:09:35,283
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]

130
00:09:49,046 --> 00:09:50,590
[JORDAN EXHALES DEEPLY]

131
00:09:51,632 --> 00:09:52,883
[SNIFFLES]

132
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:55,136
I'm sorry.

133
00:09:59,015 --> 00:10:01,434
[SNIFFLES] I'm sorry. I didn't mean to…

134
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:04,937
Um…

135
00:10:10,943 --> 00:10:12,111
[BILLY CLEARS THROAT]

136
00:10:14,196 --> 00:10:15,489
No, I did.

137
00:10:16,657 --> 00:10:17,658
Dude.

138
00:10:19,035 --> 00:10:22,538
I think it's time
for you to know the truth.

139
00:10:31,672 --> 00:10:33,382
I'm so in love with you.

140
00:10:33,466 --> 00:10:37,053
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

141
00:10:37,136 --> 00:10:38,554
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

142
00:10:43,184 --> 00:10:44,685
What are you trying to say?

143
00:10:48,439 --> 00:10:49,565
Billy.

144
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:52,443
I love you.

145
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:58,991
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

146
00:11:16,967 --> 00:11:18,302
Please.

147
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:19,970
Say something.

148
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:21,013
Please.

149
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:25,559
[EXHALES SHAKILY]

150
00:11:26,769 --> 00:11:29,355
I don't know. I don't know what to say.

151
00:11:34,527 --> 00:11:36,278
[EXHALES DEEPLY, CLEARS THROAT]

152
00:11:38,030 --> 00:11:39,115
I'm sorry

153
00:11:40,282 --> 00:11:41,784
for thinking

154
00:11:42,785 --> 00:11:44,787
that you might feel the same way.

155
00:11:44,870 --> 00:11:51,419
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

156
00:11:58,717 --> 00:12:01,137
I think you need to rest.
You should rest up.

157
00:12:04,515 --> 00:12:05,933
- Billy.
- I have to go.

158
00:12:09,311 --> 00:12:12,690
[DOOR OPENS, CREAKING]

159
00:12:12,773 --> 00:12:18,946
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

160
00:12:19,029 --> 00:12:20,489
[BREATHES HEAVILY]

161
00:12:31,375 --> 00:12:34,378
Yes. We were in a relationship before,

162
00:12:34,462 --> 00:12:36,589
but that was a long time ago.

163
00:12:36,672 --> 00:12:38,591
We've been separated for a long time.

164
00:12:38,674 --> 00:12:40,634
[OFFICER] Why didn't you report him to us?

165
00:12:41,427 --> 00:12:44,180
[KAREN] I mean, I was scared.

166
00:12:44,263 --> 00:12:46,474
What if he hurt me? Right?

167
00:12:46,557 --> 00:12:48,142
Don't you get that?

168
00:12:48,809 --> 00:12:50,436
Knowing that he's that kind of guy,

169
00:12:50,519 --> 00:12:52,897
I'm worried about what he might do to me.

170
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:54,440
And look at me.

171
00:12:54,523 --> 00:12:57,234
I'm weak. I won't be able
to stand against him.

172
00:12:58,819 --> 00:13:00,529
[KAREN INHALES DEEPLY] Well?

173
00:13:01,363 --> 00:13:03,199
Please believe me, Officer.

174
00:13:04,241 --> 00:13:05,951
I have nothing to do with it.

175
00:13:08,287 --> 00:13:15,294
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

176
00:13:23,594 --> 00:13:30,601
["AAMININ" BY JAMES REID
AND KATHRYN BERNARDO PLAYING]

177
00:13:47,576 --> 00:13:54,583
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]

178
00:14:16,855 --> 00:14:21,277
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]

179
00:14:57,104 --> 00:15:03,903
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]

180
00:15:29,053 --> 00:15:34,934
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]

181
00:16:12,930 --> 00:16:19,228
["AAMININ" CONTINUES]

182
00:16:54,513 --> 00:16:56,640
[MUSIC FADES]

183
00:16:59,852 --> 00:17:06,817
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

184
00:17:29,673 --> 00:17:35,262
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

185
00:17:48,025 --> 00:17:49,443
<i>Please.</i>

186
00:17:49,526 --> 00:17:50,652
<i>Say something.</i>

187
00:17:51,987 --> 00:17:54,782
<i>I don't know. I don't know what to say.</i>

188
00:17:58,243 --> 00:18:00,537
<i>I think you need to rest.</i>
<i>You should rest up.</i>

189
00:18:03,791 --> 00:18:05,375
<i>- Billy.</i>
<i>- I have to go.</i>

190
00:18:10,547 --> 00:18:17,179
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

191
00:18:37,449 --> 00:18:43,330
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

192
00:18:57,177 --> 00:19:04,184
[MUSIC BECOMES SOMBER]

193
00:19:27,291 --> 00:19:29,835
<i>Why don't you take the day off?</i>

194
00:19:29,918 --> 00:19:31,420
<i>I can't, Auntie.</i>

195
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:34,464
<i>Your father's heart is already recovering.</i>

196
00:19:34,548 --> 00:19:37,426
<i>Now, it seems yours is the one</i>
<i>that needs attention.</i>

197
00:19:38,510 --> 00:19:41,096
<i>- My heart is tough, Auntie.</i>
<i>- Hmm.</i>

198
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:45,517
<i>Yes, your heart might be tough,</i>
<i>but what about Jordan's heart?</i>

199
00:19:45,601 --> 00:19:46,977
<i>How is he doing?</i>

200
00:19:49,521 --> 00:19:50,772
<i>What about you, Auntie Pres?</i>

201
00:19:50,856 --> 00:19:55,444
<i>Did you notice</i>
<i>he had feelings for me?</i>

202
00:19:55,527 --> 00:19:57,362
<i>No, I didn't.</i>

203
00:19:57,446 --> 00:20:00,532
<i>That's why I was surprised</i>
<i>when you told me last night.</i>

204
00:20:00,616 --> 00:20:05,412
<i>But, Billy, you're both</i>
<i>going through a lot right now.</i>

205
00:20:05,495 --> 00:20:09,583
<i>You should be there for each other.</i>

206
00:20:10,584 --> 00:20:13,045
<i>Talk to him. Call him and check on him.</i>

207
00:20:13,128 --> 00:20:16,632
<i>I don't know how to face him right now.</i>

208
00:20:19,927 --> 00:20:21,970
<i>I don't know how.</i>

209
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:28,227
<i>Do you know that trending</i>
<i>bakery in Cavite?</i>

210
00:20:29,019 --> 00:20:30,812
<i>Its owner is a LoveLister.</i>

211
00:20:30,896 --> 00:20:33,690
<i>And the person they matched with</i>
<i>on our app</i>

212
00:20:33,774 --> 00:20:35,651
<i>is their childhood best friend!</i>

213
00:20:35,734 --> 00:20:37,903
<i>- </i>[BLAIRE] <i>Really?</i>
- [JORDAN COUGHING]

214
00:20:37,986 --> 00:20:40,322
<i>Yes, they're best friends.</i>

215
00:20:40,405 --> 00:20:43,575
<i>At first, they were just</i>
<i>teasing each other.</i>

216
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:45,619
<i>But the revelation is,</i>

217
00:20:45,702 --> 00:20:48,956
<i>the bakery owner has had</i>
<i>a long-time crush on their best friend.</i>

218
00:20:49,039 --> 00:20:50,916
<i>- How sweet!</i>
<i>- </i>[CHARM] <i>Right?</i>

219
00:20:50,999 --> 00:20:52,417
[BLAIRE] <i>That's so endearing!</i>

220
00:20:52,501 --> 00:20:54,711
[JORDAN CLEARS THROAT]

221
00:20:54,795 --> 00:20:56,546
<i>What do you think, chief?</i>

222
00:20:57,130 --> 00:20:58,131
<i>It's okay.</i>

223
00:20:59,299 --> 00:21:00,717
<i>Let's just make sure</i>

224
00:21:00,801 --> 00:21:03,887
<i>that they'd be comfortable</i>
<i>having their story featured.</i>

225
00:21:06,932 --> 00:21:09,101
<i>We looked so stupid earlier.</i>

226
00:21:12,562 --> 00:21:13,939
<i>Are you okay now?</i>

227
00:21:14,022 --> 00:21:16,191
<i>Billy, I know last night</i>
<i>wasn't the best time</i>

228
00:21:16,275 --> 00:21:18,735
<i>for me to tell you my feelings, but…</i>

229
00:21:22,114 --> 00:21:23,740
<i>what I said was true.</i>
